&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a fixed-term contract initially until 15th January 2027, with the potential for extension.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please submit your application in English.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Must be fluent, C1/C2 or native in the German language.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand &amp;amp; Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology &amp;amp; Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB PURPOSE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Copywriter, you’ll join our global Copy Team of nearly 60 creatives across the world. You&#39;ll craft content for digital channels and brand campaigns, delivering on-brand messaging that drives clicks, engagement, and brand awareness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for inspiring team players who are eager to share their expertise. You should be just as comfortable producing efficient, high-quality day-to-day work as you are developing standout ideas for award-winning campaigns and new business pitches.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a genuine passion for editing and giving critical feedback. You will be expected to uphold our clients&#39; creative standards, while continuing to push new ideas and embody DEPT®’s entrepreneurial spirit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop creative concepts and outstanding copy for digital campaigns for a leading international brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write content for a wide range of channels, including banner ads, newsletters, websites, social media campaigns, and localized adaptations across text, design, and video formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong conceptual thinking and creative writing skills to craft engaging and effective messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proofread all German-language content to ensure flawless spelling, grammar, and alignment with brand guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present your ideas convincingly to colleagues and clients, showcasing the strategic and creative thinking behind your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt global campaigns for the German market in a way that feels authentic and culturally relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct competitive and trend research to inspire fresh creative directions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and participate in creative brainstorms and other key meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate leadership, professionalism, and collaboration in all interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience as a copywriter, ideally within an agency or brand environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in multi-channel digital copywriting and brand development is a major advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in translation, transcreation, and proofreading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write compelling, sales-driven marketing copy in German is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence in working closely with designers, strategists, account managers, and clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage large-scale marketing campaigns with multiple deliverables at a fast pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the importance of consistency across touchpoints in the user journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to support campaign and copy creation is a must.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative and proactive approach to teamwork.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native-level or C1 German and excellent English skills, both written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible hybrid working policy (2 days at the office, depending on location);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lease bike options / JobRad and 25% subsidy for the Deutschlandticket.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay happy and healthy with a contribution to your health through the OpenUp platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;€30 per month - You can use the flexible package for digital food stamps and/or fitness providers/sport clubs/massage studios, internet costs, and/ or public transport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Future Bens - Exclusive access to sustainable, healthy products at attractive deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues through organised activities and celebrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reputation for doing good. DEPT® has been a Certified &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/en-gb/insight/dept-is-a-certified-b-corporation/&quot;&gt;B Corp® since 2021&lt;/a&gt; and named ‘Agency of the Year’ at both The Lovies and The Webby Awards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awesome clients. Whether big or small, local or global — at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with clients of all sizes and across all industries. And we celebrate all of our successes together!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity for possibility. We want to enable you to do what you do best and help you develop your skills further with training, development and certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global annual &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/dept-cares-day-2023/&quot;&gt;DEPT® Cares Month&lt;/a&gt; in which employees come together and donate their skills to support local charities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY DEPT®?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Disclosure&lt;/strong&gt;: At DEPT®, we use AI-assisted technology (Metaview) to capture notes and summarize interview conversations, so our interviewers can stay fully focused. Using the AI is optional, just let us know if you’d prefer it not be used.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DIVERSITY, EQUITY &amp;amp; INCLUSION&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/the-good-company/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fireblocks is the company bringing global finance onchain. Backed by over $1 billion in capital, we are the premier digital asset infrastructure provider trusted by thousands of industry-defining financial institutions, including banks, payment providers, fintechs, and global corporates such as BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Western Union, Stripe, and Revolut. Built for institutional scale and security, our enterprise-grade platform and network have powered over $14 trillion in digital asset transfers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sales Engineer, Banking is a technically credible, commercially aware member of the EMEA SE team, responsible for the full technical sales cycle across banking opportunities in Western and Central Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a generalist SE role. You will be expected to engage deeply with treasury operations leads, custody technologists, CISOs, and risk committees inside Tier 1 and Tier 2 banks. You will need to understand how institutional banking technology works — core banking platforms, custody and settlement infrastructure, ISO 20022 and SWIFT messaging, and post-trade workflows — and be able to position Fireblocks clearly within that context.&amp;nbsp;You will work closely with Banking-aligned Sales Directors across your region, taking primary responsibility for technical qualification, PoC delivery, RFP responses, and solution design from first engagement through to onboarding handoff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Pre-Sales&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical qualification for banking opportunities, distinguishing genuine digital asset programmes from exploratory noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver tailored product demonstrations to technical and executive audiences across custody, settlement, treasury, and compliance use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope, design, and deliver Proofs of Concept in bank environments — including navigating infosec review, sandbox provisioning, and API integration testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and own RFP, RFI, and DDQ responses for banking prospects, maintaining accuracy against Fireblocks&#39; external security and compliance attestations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present Fireblocks&#39; security architecture to CISOs, CROs, risk committees, and product and business line leads with appropriate institutional credibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Design &amp;amp; Client Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate institutional banking requirements — custody flows, settlement logic, treasury management, regulatory reporting — into Fireblocks solution architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with bank technology teams on API integration patterns, core banking middleware, and operational workflow design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-develop technical account plans with Sales Directors, identifying the path from initial engagement to production deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to deal strategy on competitive situations, particularly against technology-first custody competitors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the banking client in internal product and roadmap discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute reusable technical content — solution briefs, reference architectures, PoC templates — that scale across the Banking vertical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding handoff to Professional Services, ensuring continuity from sales into delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the EMEA SE enablement programme, contributing to banking-specific sessions and peer knowledge transfer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–8 years in a pre-sales, solutions engineering, or technical consulting role, selling into or supporting Tier 1 or Tier 2 banks, financial market infrastructure, or capital markets firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise sales cycles in regulated financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable track record of scoping and delivering PoCs or technical pilots in bank environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience authoring RFP/RFI responses and engaging with bank procurement, legal, and infosec processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to digital asset, tokenisation, or blockchain initiatives whether from a technology vendor, infrastructure provider, or within a bank&#39;s innovation function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of institutional banking architecture: core banking platforms (Temenos, Finastra, Murex, Calypso or similar), custody infrastructure, or post-trade settlement systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial messaging standards: ISO 20022, SWIFT MT/MX, or equivalent settlement and payment protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with API-led integration patterns; able to engage credibly in technical discussions with bank engineering and middleware teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of cryptographic key management concepts, hardware security modules, or MPC/TSS architecture (formal training provided)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of MiCA, DORA, or equivalent EMEA regulatory requirements as they affect digital asset operations in banks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible with senior institutional stakeholders CISO, CTO, Head of Digital Assets, treasury operations leads, and product and business line owners — not only with technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured, precise communicator: able to write clearly, present confidently, and adapt register for technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially aware: understands deal economics, qualification discipline, and what constitutes productive SE engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed and organised, capable of running multiple active opportunities simultaneously without close supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A European language an advantage&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For employees hired to work from the EU, Fireblocks is required by law to include a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. This range is specific to&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; Germany&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;and takes into consideration a wide range of factors that are reviewed when making a hiring decision, such as years of experience, skills, and other business needs. It is not typical for a candidate to be hired at or near the top of the pay range and each compensation decision is dependent on each individual case. A reasonable base salary range estimate for this position is&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;€80,000 – €110,000. The base salary is one component of the total compensation package, which for some roles may include a target bonus, a very competitive equity grant, and very generous benefits. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;While we believe competitive compensation is a critical aspect of your decision to join us, we do hope you also spend time considering why our mission and culture are right for you. We are creating something transformational here, and we hope you are as excited about the future as we are.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
